# Moga Dev SpecKit Context

- Treat `.specify/memory/constitution.md` as the architecture and process authority.
- Before specifying, planning, testing, or implementing, read the relevant files in
  `.specify/memory/` and inspect the applicable Salesforce metadata and existing code.
- Use real API names from `force-app/main/default`; never invent objects, fields, statuses,
  integrations, product combinations, approval limits, or mandatory-document rules.
- Record conflicts among approved requirements, repository behavior, metadata, and observed
  org behavior as discrepancies. Ask for resolution instead of silently choosing a source.
- Keep secrets, tokens, OTP values, personal data, bureau payloads, and full PAN/Aadhaar values
  out of source, specifications, logs, tests, screenshots, and dashboard data.
- Use the workflow `/speckit-specify` → `/speckit-clarify` as needed → `/speckit-plan` →
  `/speckit-tasks` → `/speckit-analyze` → `/speckit-implement`.
- Do not treat an integration handler, mock, or stub as evidence of production readiness.
- Update `docs/progress-tracker.json` only for identified epics/stories with traceable evidence.

